---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Faq from '../components/seo/Faq.astro';
import '../components/seo/seo.css';
import { pageViewer } from '../site/viewer';
const { viewer, csrf } = await pageViewer(Astro);
const faq: [string, string][] = [
  [
    'Is this a guaranteed way to earn money playing games?',
    'No. Applying does not guarantee approval, orders or income. Earnings depend on eligible sessions you actually complete.',
  ],
  [
    'How much of a session goes to the teammate?',
    'The standard pricing calculation starts from a 60 percent share of the session amount after applicable discounts, converted to USD at the reference rate with cent rounding. The desk shows the actual amount and any adjustments.',
  ],
  [
    'What is the payout minimum?',
    'The current code sets a USD 25 weekly payout minimum. Smaller amounts carry forward. Holds and required payout details can delay payment.',
  ],
  [
    'How are teammates paid?',
    'Manual payout details support bank, Wise and PayPal. Stripe Connect is a separate supported rail when enabled and ready. Confirm which route is available in your desk.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I apply for Social sessions?',
    'Social orders require Gamer Girl service access. Follow the application process and review the friendly-company boundaries.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I play on a customer’s account?',
    'You play using your own account and follow publisher rules. Customers keep control of their accounts and credentials.',
  ],
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Get Paid to Play Games as a Duoly Teammate | Duoly"
  description="Apply to get paid to play games as a Duoly teammate. Learn the real session share, USD 25 payout minimum, application requirements and service boundaries."
  indexing="index, follow"
  viewer={viewer}
  csrf={csrf}
>
  <article class="seo-page">
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
        { name: 'Become a teammate', path: '/get-paid-to-play-games' },
      ]}
    />
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Teammate applications</p>
      <h1>Get paid to play games as a Duoly teammate</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Apply to provide paid gaming, coaching or friendly Social sessions.
        Duoly is a session marketplace, with no guaranteed orders, earnings or
        fixed hourly wage.
      </p>
      <a class="cta" href="/apply">
        Apply to become a teammate
      </a>
      <p>
        The standard session-share calculation starts at 60 percent. Your desk
        shows the actual session amount and payout status.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section>
      <h2>What the work involves</h2>
      <p>
        You provide the service a customer booked. A gaming teammate joins the
        agreed mode, communicates respectfully and follows the session unit. A
        coach explains decisions and gives focused feedback. A Gamer Girl may
        provide game-specific sessions or, with the relevant access, Social
        voice company. Each format needs a clear scope and the ability to keep a
        session comfortable.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is different from reward apps that pay for installs, surveys or
        playtime. You earn through eligible customer sessions you complete.
        Strong gameplay alone is not the entire job: listening, punctual
        communication, honest service claims and handling a difficult match
        calmly all matter. Do not apply on the assumption that simply leaving a
        game open creates earnings.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>How session share and payouts work</h2>
      <p>
        The standard pricing function calculates a teammate share from 60
        percent of the discounted session amount, converts it at the EUR to USD
        reference rate, rounds to cents and subtracts one cent, with a USD 0.99
        floor in that calculation. Customer display currency and the teammate
        USD amount are separate. Account-specific discounts or later ledger
        adjustments mean a headline catalog price is not a guaranteed take-home
        figure.
      </p>
      <p>
        Payouts are organised in weekly lines. The current code sets the minimum
        at USD 25; smaller amounts carry into a later week. Required payout
        details must be completed, and holds or unresolved order issues can
        affect whether money is payable. An earnings entry, a scheduled payout
        and funds received are different states. Check the desk rather than
        assuming that a completed game means an immediate transfer.
      </p>
      <p>
        The supported manual payout details include bank, Wise and PayPal.
        Stripe Connect is also implemented as a conditional rail for accounts
        that complete its verification and have the required capabilities
        enabled. Its availability depends on platform configuration and your
        account status. Do not assume a specific rail, transfer currency or
        arrival time before checking the current setup with Duoly.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Prepare an honest application</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 and able to follow the platform and publisher
        rules. Describe the games and services you can genuinely provide, your
        region and your communication preferences. Use accurate rank or
        experience evidence where relevant. A coaching application should
        explain what you can teach, rather than relying on a high rank as the
        only proof of teaching ability.
      </p>
      <p>
        Follow the current <a href="/apply">application form</a> for the
        requested fields and evidence. Application review determines access, and
        submitting does not guarantee acceptance. Some service categories
        require separate access. Social orders are restricted to teammates with
        Gamer Girl access; they are friendly company only, never dating,
        romantic or sexual services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep examples specific. For Valorant, say whether you can explain
        controller utility, entry timing or VOD decisions. For Rocket League,
        distinguish playing Doubles from teaching recoveries. For a Social
        application, describe how you would keep a voice session welcoming while
        setting boundaries. Use only your own work and evidence you are allowed
        to share.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>A sensible first-session routine</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Read the service, unit and customer preferences before accepting an
          eligible order. Check region, mode and legitimate queue compatibility.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use the order chat to coordinate. Confirm the activity and voice
          setup, then deliver the session as booked using your own accounts.
        </li>
        <li>
          Follow the completion process and review the earnings record in your
          desk. Use support for disagreements instead of arranging a private
          payment.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Keep a record through the platform tools and never promise wins, a new
        rank or personal contact outside the booking. You are responsible for
        understanding your own tax and reporting obligations. Ask Duoly about
        payout setup before depending on any expected transfer.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Faq items={faq} />
    <nav class="related" aria-label="Related pages">
      <h2>Before you apply</h2>
      <a href="/apply">Teammate application</a>
      <a href="/games">Services by game</a>
      <a href="/games/social">Social boundaries</a>
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
      <a href="/contact">Ask the Duoly team</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
